{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01An2qVBdZf8oaVTeeHa18Ha","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"vitest testNamePattern full name separator suite test space \" > \"\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"vitest.dev\",\"url\":\"https://vitest.dev/config/testnamepattern\"},{\"title\":\"docs.w3cub.com\",\"url\":\"https://docs.w3cub.com/vitest/config/testnamepattern\"},{\"title\":\"main.vitest.dev\",\"url\":\"https://main.vitest.dev/config/testnamepattern\"},{\"title\":\"Test Filtering\",\"url\":\"https://vitest.dev/guide/filtering\"},{\"title\":\"docs.w3cub.com\",\"url\":\"https://docs.w3cub.com/vitest/guide/filtering\"},{\"title\":\"main.vitest.dev\",\"url\":\"https://main.vitest.dev/guide/filtering\"},{\"title\":\"This documentation covers Vitest v2 (old version). For the latest version, see\",\"url\":\"https://v2.vitest.dev/guide/filtering\"},{\"title\":\"next.tangled.org\",\"url\":\"https://next.tangled.org/vitest.dev/vitest/blob/v3/docs/guide/filtering.md\"},{\"title\":\"next.tangled.org\",\"url\":\"https://next.tangled.org/vitest.dev/vitest/blob/v2/docs/guide/filtering.md\"},{\"title\":\"test suite\",\"url\":\"https://v3.vitest.dev/advanced/api/test-suite\"}]\n\nThe separator is `\" > \"` in current Vitest docs. Matching is done against the full name, which is the enclosing suite names plus the test name joined with that separator. The pattern is matched against the test's full name: the enclosing suite names and the test name joined with ' > ' (the same string shown in the reporter output).\n\nFor a test nested in a `describe`, you can filter with the full string or just the test name. The test below has the full name math > adds, so it is matched by -t 'math > adds' or -t adds.\n\nThe separator changed in a recent version. The docs carry a warning: Before Vitest 5, the segments were joined with a single space (math adds) to mirror Jest. So if you're on an older Vitest, you may need `-t 'math adds'` instead of `-t 'math > adds'`. Check your installed version if a pattern isn't matching.\n\nThe CLI flag is `-t` or `--testNamePattern`, and the option also works in config. You can also use the -t, --testNamePattern <pattern> option to filter tests by full name.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f8985615-1507-44ff-b333-8fd7e96f0ee8","uuid":"0d77000b-3a10-4d6a-b9e6-33f5caf2e060","timestamp":"2026-10-08T12:38:20.434Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"vitest testNamePattern full name separator suite test space \" > \"","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01HncGoVMfxwaDhHqCWSwhqZ","content":[{"title":"vitest.dev","url":"https://vitest.dev/config/testnamepattern"},{"title":"docs.w3cub.com","url":"https://docs.w3cub.com/vitest/config/testnamepattern"},{"title":"main.vitest.dev","url":"https://main.vitest.dev/config/testnamepattern"},{"title":"Test Filtering","url":"https://vitest.dev/guide/filtering"},{"title":"docs.w3cub.com","url":"https://docs.w3cub.com/vitest/guide/filtering"},{"title":"main.vitest.dev","url":"https://main.vitest.dev/guide/filtering"},{"title":"This documentation covers Vitest v2 (old version). For the latest version, see","url":"https://v2.vitest.dev/guide/filtering"},{"title":"next.tangled.org","url":"https://next.tangled.org/vitest.dev/vitest/blob/v3/docs/guide/filtering.md"},{"title":"next.tangled.org","url":"https://next.tangled.org/vitest.dev/vitest/blob/v2/docs/guide/filtering.md"},{"title":"test suite","url":"https://v3.vitest.dev/advanced/api/test-suite"}]},"The separator is `\" > \"` in current Vitest docs. Matching is done against the full name, which is the enclosing suite names plus the test name joined with that separator. The pattern is matched against the test's full name: the enclosing suite names and the test name joined with ' > ' (the same string shown in the reporter output).\n\nFor a test nested in a `describe`, you can filter with the full string or just the test name. The test below has the full name math > adds, so it is matched by -t 'math > adds' or -t adds.\n\nThe separator changed in a recent version. The docs carry a warning: Before Vitest 5, the segments were joined with a single space (math adds) to mirror Jest. So if you're on an older Vitest, you may need `-t 'math adds'` instead of `-t 'math > adds'`. Check your installed version if a pattern isn't matching.\n\nThe CLI flag is `-t` or `--testNamePattern`, and the option also works in config. You can also use the -t, --testNamePattern <pattern> option to filter tests by full name."],"durationSeconds":4.7088778,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01An2qVBdZf8oaVTeeHa18Ha","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
