{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfpnP54VBM5UhkvZpzATj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"In current Vitest (v5 and later), `testNamePattern` (`-t`) is matched against the test's full name. That's the enclosing `describe` names and the test name joined with **`\" > \"`** (space, greater-than, space), the same string the reporter prints. So an `adds` test inside a `math` suite is `math > adds`, and `-t 'math > adds'` matches it. `-t adds` also matches, because the pattern only has to match part of the name.\n\nThis changed in Vitest 5. Earlier versions joined the names with a single space (`math adds`) to match Jest. I had expected the space separator, so I checked the current docs. On Vitest 4 or older, use `-t 'math adds'` instead.\n\nSources:\n- [Vitest config: testNamePattern](https://vitest.dev/config/testnamepattern)\n- [Vitest guide: Test Filtering](https://vitest.dev/guide/filtering)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":417,"cache_read_input_tokens":5752,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":417},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f8985615-1507-44ff-b333-8fd7e96f0ee8","uuid":"e8c81697-740c-4958-8942-2809f0f15496","timestamp":"2026-10-08T12:38:31.906Z","request_id":"req_011CfpnP4idzVcjoiiAbyVCa"}
